# ── Un-ignore rules first: in gitignore the LAST matching rule wins, so anything below
#    this block can still re-exclude what it needs to.

# The global gitignore excludes `*~` (editor backup files). `Skills~` is a real directory that
# must ship: Unity ignores `~`-suffixed folders, which is exactly why the skills live there.
!Skills~/
!library/Skills~/
!library/Skills~/**

# NOTE: there are deliberately no Unity `Library/` `Temp/` `Logs/` rules in this file.
# This repo is not a Unity project — `library/` IS the shipped package. macOS git runs with
# core.ignorecase=true, so a `Library/` rule silently matches `library/`: already-tracked files
# keep working while every NEW file added to the package stops being tracked. Nothing looks wrong
# until someone clones and half the package is missing.

# ── Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

# ── macOS
.DS_Store

# Personal working files — reports, scratch
Reports/
